- Story & Context: Recorded live during the 1995 monsoon season at the contested border channel between Sector 4 and the old shipping yards, this track captures the moment Som-O jammed her bass neck into an iron lock-gate while a TR-909 beat thumped from a floating crate. Customs inspectors were so mesmerized by the low-frequency glass slides echoing off the concrete walls that they let eighty unregistered barges pass into the city without paying customs fees. "If the water doesn't pay the toll, the bass takes the river back," spat Som-O into a wet microphone as the lock gates opened. The track became the founding anthem for the entire sub-delta movement, its continuous bass slide mimicking the sound of rusted iron dragging across gravel under forty feet of water.
